# cfront output. `cmd/c++lib/mkfile' generates every .c from the matching
# .cpp under external/cfront-C4/lib, and its own CLEANFILES says "*.c".
# All 40 were once COMMITTED AT ZERO BYTES, so a fresh checkout compiled
# 40 empty translation units into libc++.a and the build reported success
# -- a check that cannot fail.
sys/src/ape/cmd/c++lib/*.c

# cfrontsz-probe's two generated files were ignored here and that was
# wrong: git IS the only channel to the VM, and the probe exists to be
# run under pcc there. An ignored generated file is a file the VM never
# sees, which is exactly what happened -- `pcc ... cfrontsz-probe.c'
# answered `Can't open input file'. They are committed now; regenerate
# and re-commit when cfront's main.c changes.  (Not the same shape as
# the 40 zero-byte c++lib files above: those were an INPUT to mk, which
# therefore never regenerated them. These two are in nobody's OFILES.)
